    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change derives an owner's `locality` from their city and exposes it on `GET /api/owners/{id}`. I kept structural impact low by adding the behaviour as a small, self-contained unit rather than growing any existing class:\n\n1. **New `util/Locality.java`** \u2014 a tiny cohesive class holding the fixed city-to-region table (`Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD`) with a single `of(city)` method (CC 1) returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"`. It carries essentially no surrounding complexity, mirroring the existing `Household` util.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line delegating to `Locality.of(owner.getCity())`, exactly matching the existing expression-based derivations (`householdId`, `membershipTier`). No method body was enlarged.\n\nNo existing method's logic was touched, so no large class pays its WMC for this feature. Both new acceptance tests (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity`, `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown`) and the full suite pass.",
